<InstitutionalPage
  title="Corrections"
  eyebrow="Accountability"
  description="Material factual corrections are disclosed on the affected Nuvellum article."
  intro="When a published factual error materially changes what a reader should understand, the correction should be visible."
  note="Minor typographical fixes may be made without a correction note when they do not alter meaning."
>
  <h2>Material corrections</h2>
  <p>Material factual corrections are disclosed on the affected article. The purpose is not to preserve the original mistake; it is to leave the reader with an accurate record and a visible explanation when the change matters.</p>
  <h2>Minor edits</h2>
  <p>Spelling, punctuation, formatting and other non-substantive fixes may be made without a correction note when they do not change meaning, attribution or the substance of the reporting.</p>
  <h2>Raise a correction</h2>
  <p>If you believe a Nuvellum article contains a factual error, use the <a class="int-action" href="/contact">contact page</a>. Include the article title and the specific passage at issue.</p>
</InstitutionalPage>
